      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FLYING SWAGMAN (5) has the clearest winning profile after being beaten half a length at Ascot last start as a short odds-on favourite, and that came after a respectable eighth in the Listed Belgravia Stakes. Has the speed to offset the tricky barrier and he can go one better this time. THE MIGHTY BELL (7) is the main danger, having won a CL1 at Bunbury two back before finishing second there last start. Likely to get back again from the draw, but her two ratings this time in stack up and another forward showing is anticipated. WE LOVE CHARLIE (4) resumes with three wins from six starts, trialled second at Albany in a solid effort and she can make an impression right away. INTIMIDATION TIME (6) is race fit, drawn barrier 1 and comes off a third at this venue after winning a Mdn at Bunbury. Can sit up front and be tough to reel in. I'M A SOULMAN (8) is third-up now and coming back in trip looks a good move.",
